# The pipeline, the gates and the build inputs belong to the build-admins team (docs#1237), as in the
# library repository: changing any of these needs a build admin's approval of the pull request's latest
# commit, unless a build admin opened it (the library's GOVERNANCE.md, "Roles":
# https://github.com/whizbang-lib/whizbang/blob/develop/GOVERNANCE.md#roles). The ruleset does not require
# a code owner's review, since an author cannot approve their own pull request; the Gate · Pipeline owner
# check (.github/scripts/Test-PipelineOwner.ps1, the library's gate ported) reads this file instead.
# Maintainers and committers can propose such a change; a build admin approves it. The gate reads this
# file from the base branch, so a pull request cannot loosen it for itself. Patterns are plain paths: a
# wildcard fails the gate rather than being guessed at. Everything else needs no particular owner.
# Every pattern must match a file (.github/scripts/tests/CodeOwners.Tests.ps1).
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Workflows, composite actions, Dependabot, this file
/.github/                   @whizbang-lib/build-admins

# Build and gate scripts (check-linked-change.mjs is the "Gate · Linked change" decision)
/src/scripts/               @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/build-search-index.sh      @whizbang-lib/build-admins

# Dependencies and toolchain
/package.json               @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/pnpm-lock.yaml             @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/pnpm-workspace.yaml        @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/.nvmrc                     @whizbang-lib/build-admins

# Site build configuration and the custom domain
/angular.json               @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/tsconfig.json              @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/tsconfig.app.json          @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/CNAME                      @whizbang-lib/build-admins

# Read the Docs build
/.readthedocs.yaml          @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/mkdocs.yml                 @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/rtd/                       @whizbang-lib/build-admins
